From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000075 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xPDFSDK Automation <dev@xpdfsdk.local>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 14:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] r25-0075: add holder-owned immutable RenderProgram v2 boundary

Start the replacement RenderProgram architecture from the correctness baseline:
r25 plus the 0051 page-dimensions API. This patch deliberately has no dependency
on the experimental 0053-0074 RenderPlan stack.

The long-lived rendering representation needs the same lifetime as the parsed
page or Form holder. Add that ownership boundary now, before adding recording,
commands, replay, caches, or renderer hooks:

* Add an opaque `VeloceRenderProgram` type in the page layer. A future parser-
  owned builder is the only class allowed to construct a program.
* Let `CPDF_PageObjectHolder` own an optional `unique_ptr<const
  VeloceRenderProgram>`. The const ownership contract means the holder only
  receives sealed immutable programs; replay cannot mutate shared program data.
* Expose narrow get, install, and reset operations for parser completion and
  future edit invalidation. No raw page-object pointer is stored in the program
  boundary.

This revision is intentionally behavior-neutral. The optional pointer remains
null because no builder exists yet. It adds no page scan, classification,
allocation, cache, render-path branch, lock, log, JNI/API change, or pixel
change. Patch 0076 will add parser-time recording behind this ownership
contract.
